# Pragmatic Clean Architecture

BlinkGuard uses pragmatic CA, with the Electron entry reduced to composition. Prefer extracting when a boundary is clear and testable; do not invent one-interface-per-button layers.

## Where things go

| Kind of change | Put it in |
|---|---|
| Pure policy / formula (no I/O) | `electron/domain/` or `python/.../domain/` |
| Cross-cutting contracts (IPC, prefs, backup, camera, blink-stats, i18n, …) | `shared/` (TS only; no Electron imports) |
| Reminder / exercise / look-away / stats / calibration-nudge / camera-capture-status / snooze-all / session-recap / focus / preferences orchestration | `electron/application/` (+ small set of `ports/`) |
| Store, windows, IPC, sidecar, lifecycle, shortcuts, tray, sound, OS toasts | `electron/infrastructure/` |
| Dependency wiring and app startup | `electron/main.ts` only (`composition-root`) |
| Settings UI state / controls | `src/features/<feature>/{model,ui}/` |
| Shared React controls | `src/components/` |
| Preload bridge usage from React | `src/shared/ipc/` |
| Popup DOM behavior / CSS | `public/js/`, `public/css/` |
| Sidecar detection math / camera I/O / transport | `python/blink_detector_package/{domain,application,infrastructure}/` |

## Dependency rule

- Domain and `shared/` must not import Electron, React, Node `child_process`/`fs` process APIs, or OpenCV.
- Application depends on domain/shared and **ports** only — not on `BrowserWindow`, `electron-store`, or spawn details.
- Infrastructure implements ports and may import Electron/Node.
- React features depend on `renderer-ipc`, not on main-process modules.

## Anti-patterns

- Importing `electron` / `BrowserWindow` / `ipcMain` from `electron/domain` or `electron/application`
- Creating a port + adapter for a one-line getter with a single caller
- Rebuilding popup UIs in React (dual UI stays split)
- Putting preference defaults only in `main.ts` instead of `shared/preferences.ts`
- Changing sidecar handshake status strings on one side only
- Adding feature logic, BrowserWindow factories, IPC handlers, or timers back into `main.ts`

## Current Electron map

- `domain/`: `reminder-policy`, `reminder-prompt-policy`, `focus-policy`, `session-activity-policy`, `blink-rate-coaching` (helpers), `calibration-freshness`, `session-recap-policy`
- `application/`: `AppRuntimeState`; preferences, reminder, exercise, look-away, tracking-session, blink-stats, settings-profiles, calibration-nudge, camera-capture-status, snooze-all, snooze-token-prompt, session-recap-service, focus-pause, session-pause, preference-actions, deferred-tracking-restore; ports for storage/runtime/stats/focus/notification/session-activity
- `infrastructure/`: IPC registration, BrowserWindow controller, sidecar spawn/protocol, lifecycle/power, cleanup, shortcuts, tray (`tray/`), sound, OS toasts (`notifications/`), paths/store/logging
- `main.ts`: creates those collaborators, connects callbacks (incl. deferred tracking restore on `shellReady`), and starts the app. Order: see `composition-root` (hush orchestrators / `trayRef` before controllers).
